  "summary": "Four studies directly apply graph neural networks (message‑passing relational graph models) to fraud detection. Fischer et al. (2023) achieve an F1 of 0.80 on the GridWatch dataset, the strongest recent performance [V0052]. Chen et al. (2020) report 0.94 accuracy on LedgerGuard, the highest absolute metric but on an older benchmark [V0049]. El‑Sayed et al. (2022) obtain AUROC 0.73 on ToxiBench, showing moderate results on a different benchmark [V0051]. Duarte et al. (2021) evaluate on CellLife with MAE 0.66, indicating regression‑style evaluation on fraud‑related scores [V0050]. A fifth GNN study, though not fraud‑focused, applies the same message‑passing approach to hate‑speech detection with AUROC 0.93 on ToxiBench, illustrating the broader applicability of the method [V0097].",
